DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261212T130000
DTSTAMP:20261113T202054Z
UID:savethebay-1406021@local-events
DESCRIPTION:It is planting season! All the work we’ve done throughout th
 e year collecting seed\, growing and caring for our precious native plants
  has been leading to this moment right as the seasonal rains are here. We 
 hope you will join us in putting these plants in the ground at the Palo Al
 to Baylands\, where they will help restore vulnerable bay fill lands back 
 into healthy and resilient salt marsh habitat for all.\n\nAccessibility: T
 his program involves walking on paved and gravel trails and working on a s
 loped dirt surface. There is a porta-potty a 10 minute walk away from the 
 site. Planting involves kneeling or sitting on potentially uneven or muddy
  terrain. Parking is directly adjacent to the planting area.\n\nPlease dre
 ss according to the weather\, bring a water bottle and a snack. Gloves\, h
 and…\n\nSave The Bay recommends ages 8+\; under-16 must be accompanied b
 y a parent/guardian and sign a waiver. 6-year-old eligibility varies per e
 vent — confirm with STB before registering.\n\nAges: 8+ recommended (6+ 
 with parent\, per-event confirmation)\nRegistration: required\nSource: htt
 ps://savesfbay.org/event/native-planting-at-palo-alto-baylands-ssnvyaw/\nL
 ast synced: 2026-11-13 12:20 PST
LOCATION:San Francisco Bay Area
URL:https://savesfbay.org/event/native-planting-at-palo-alto-baylands-ssnv
 yaw/
END:VEVENT
